DATASET DESCRIPTION

Overview
--------

The Marketing Campaign Dataset contains approximately 200,000 records
and 16 features related to marketing campaigns and their performance.

The dataset includes information about campaign types, target audiences,
marketing channels, conversion rates, acquisition costs, ROI, customer
segments, engagement, clicks, impressions, locations, languages, and
campaign dates.


Dataset Information
-------------------

Dataset Name     : Marketing Campaign Dataset
File Format      : TXT
Number of Records: Approximately 200,000
Number of Features: 16
Domain           : Marketing Analytics
Main Metric      : ROI


Dataset Features
----------------

Campaign_ID
Unique identifier for each marketing campaign.

Company
Company associated with the campaign.

Campaign_Type
Type of marketing campaign.

Target_Audience
Target audience of the campaign.

Duration
Duration of the marketing campaign.

Channel_Used
Marketing channel used for the campaign.

Conversion_Rate
Rate of users who successfully converted.

Acquisition_Cost
Cost associated with acquiring customers.

ROI
Return on Investment generated by the campaign.

Location
Location associated with the campaign.

Language
Language used in the campaign.

Clicks
Number of clicks generated by the campaign.

Impressions
Number of times the campaign was displayed.

Engagement_Score
Score representing customer engagement with the campaign.

Customer_Segment
Customer segment targeted by the campaign.

Date
Date associated with the campaign.


Purpose of the Dataset
----------------------

The dataset is used to analyze marketing campaign performance and
understand the relationship between campaign characteristics, marketing
channels, customer segments, acquisition costs, engagement, conversion
rates, and ROI.


Data Usage
----------

The dataset is used as the input data for the Python data analysis project.

It is loaded into Google Colab using Pandas and is then used for data
cleaning, exploratory data analysis, visualization, statistical analysis,
and machine learning.


Data Access
-----------

The dataset is stored separately from the main GitHub project repository
and is accessed from Google Drive while running the Google Colab notebook.
